l distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{Y|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+0+4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545758 17592186576411 false] [17592186542228 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row 