ft(2g-\\frac{1}{5}\\right) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\n2g=0\\,\\text{or}\\,2g-\\frac{1}{5}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\ng=0\\,\\text{or}\\,g=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $g=0$ and $g=\\frac{1}{10}.$" 13194139545758 17592186576411 true] [17592186557215 1074 "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(1-x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are  $x=0$ and  $x=1.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=1.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={2\\pi (\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\text{ }-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\pi [(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5})-0] \\\\  & =2\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{20}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545758 17592186576411 false] [17592186557215 1074 "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(1-x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are  $x=0$ and  $x=1.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=1.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={2\\pi \\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\text{ }-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\right)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\left[\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\\right)-0\\right] \\\\  & =2\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{20}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545758 17592186576411 true]