 that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{t},\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}-1}{t},\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545758 17592186576411 false] [17592186563649 1074 "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =\\left\\langle \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{t},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{t}^{2}-2t+2}{t+1},\\,2\\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{(2t)},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\frac{{0}^{2}-2\\cdot 0+2}{0+1},\\,2\\cdot 1,\\,0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨2,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the second component of $\\lim_{t\\to 0}f(t)$ we used a special limit $\\lim_{u\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡u}{u}=1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =\\left\\langle \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2t}-1}{t},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(t+1)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{({e}^{2t}-1)^{′}}{(t)^{′}},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(t+1)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =\\left\\langle \\lim_{t\\to 0}\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{1},\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\lim_{t\\to 0}(t+1)\\right\\rangle  \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{0},\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,0+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for the first component of $\\lim_{t\\to 0}g(t)$ we used L'Hopital's Rule.\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{t\\to 0}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & =\\lim_{t\\to 0}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545758 1759